{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7272557","formula":"C₁₃H₁₅N₃","hill":"C13H15N3","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":15.0,"N":3.0},"names":{"en":"Quipazine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Quipazine, also known as 1-(2-quinolinyl)piperazine (2-QP), is a serotonergic drug of the arylpiperazine family and an analogue of 1-(2-pyridinyl)piperazine which is used in scientific research. It was first described in the 1960s and was originally intended as an antidepressant but was never developed or marketed for medical use. The effects of quipazine in humans include nausea, vomiting, gastrointestinal disturbances, diarrhea, and, at higher doses, psychedelic effects."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":5011,"mass":213.28,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CN(CCN1)C2=NC3=CC=CC=C3C=C2","inchikey":"XRXDAJYKGWNHTQ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-piperazin-1-ylquinoline","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"5011","atoms":31,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.866,"y":0.096,"z":-0.05,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.642,"y":-0.517,"z":0.201,"el":"N"},{"x":0.342,"y":-0.736,"z":0.134,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.367,"y":-1.225,"z":-0.452,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.695,"y":0.824,"z":0.918,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.84,"y":-1.14,"z":-0.851,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.156,"y":0.834,"z":0.471,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.484,"y":0.314,"z":-0.082,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.051,"y":1.6,"z":-0.334,"el":"C"},{"x":1.671,"y":-0.518,"z":0.1,"el":"C"},{"x":2.209,"y":0.762,"z":-0.151,"el":"C"},{"x":1.318,"y":1.821,"z":-0.368,"el":"C"},{"x":2.556,"y":-1.57,"z":0.316,"el":"C"},{"x":3.601,"y":0.953,"z":-0.179,"el":"C"},{"x":3.94,"y":-1.38,"z":0.288,"el":"C"},{"x":4.463,"y":-0.117,"z":0.041,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.24,"y":-1.934,"z":0.377,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.8,"y":-1.608,"z":-1.31,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.365,"y":1.862,"z":1.037,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.604,"y":0.342,"z":1.9,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.946,"y":-0.575,"